# FlowEnergetic / CONSTANT-VOLUME BURN of the idealised condensed explosive  (Hydro2, energetic.on = 1)
#
# A periodic box of unreacted explosive (phase 0) with a trace of products (phase 1), at rest; the ignition
# pressure is set to 0 so that the whole box burns with  d lambda/dt = -k sqrt(lambda)  (lambda = 0 at t = 2/k = 1 us).
# Explosive: Petitpas et al., Shock Waves 19 (2009) 377, as used by Wallis, Barton & Nikiforakis, Comput. Struct.
# 254 (2021) 106578, Table 2 -- reactant: stiffened gas gamma = 4, p_inf = 1 GPa, rho_0 = 1600 kg/m^3;
# products: ideal gas gamma = 3;  Q = 3.68 MJ/kg.  SI units.
#
# Closed forms (mass, volume and energy are conserved; all of the box ends as products at the initial density):
#   lambda(t) = (1 - k t/2)^2                               until t = 2/k
#   rho E     = rho E(0) + Q rho_0 (1 - lambda)
#   p_end     = (gamma_p - 1) [ (p_0 + gamma_r p_inf)/(gamma_r - 1) + rho_0 Q ] = 1.4444e10 Pa
# Check:  python3 tests/FlowEnergetic/reference/burn_check.py <run_dir>
